    "title": "pandas.Index.dtype — pandas 3.0.5 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Index.dtype#\n\n- Index.dtype[source]#\n- Return the dtype object of the underlying data. See also \n  - `Index.inferred_type`\n  - Return a string of the type inferred from the values.\n Examples >>> idx = pd.Index([1, 2, 3]) >>> idx Index([1, 2, 3], dtype='int64') >>> idx.dtype dtype('int64')",
